{"type":"standard","title":"Westphalian language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Westphalian language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q505655","titles":{"canonical":"Westphalian_language","normalized":"Westphalian language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Westphalian language</span></span>"},"pageid":201259,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Wippe_Mai_2008_1.jpg/330px-Wippe_Mai_2008_1.jpg","width":330,"height":247},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/Wippe_Mai_2008_1.jpg","width":1063,"height":797},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1352178133","tid":"7a5c954c-463e-11f1-b496-23c30bb774e0","timestamp":"2026-05-02T15:49:18Z","description":"Low German dialects spoken in Germany","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westphalian_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westphalian_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westphalian_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Westphalian_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westphalian_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Westphalian_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westphalian_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Westphalian_language"}},"extract":"Westphalian or Westfalish is one of the major dialect groups of Low German. Its most salient feature is its diphthongization. For example, speakers say iäten instead of etten or äten for \"to eat\".","extract_html":"<p><b>Westphalian</b> or <b>Westfalish</b> is one of the major dialect groups of Low German. Its most salient feature is its diphthongization. For example, speakers say <span><i lang=\"wep\">iäten</i></span> instead of <span><i lang=\"gmw\">etten</i></span> or <span><i lang=\"gmw\">äten</i></span> for \"to eat\".</p>"}